{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And He blotted out every existence.</b> This is a great general principle for all living beings that were blotted out in those boiling waters — וימחו מן הארץ, 'they were blotted out from the earth': they were blotted out from the earth, and their forces from the heavens. Now you already know that all the forces have an appointed source and an activity among the lower beings, and since they were blotted out from the activity of the earth, behold, their force and appointed source above was annulled. The intention is not that the supernal forces themselves were annulled in the Flood, but rather that their flow ceased — they no longer flowed downward, nor did they receive flow from above, from the central line that bestows upon all recipients. And since all those who draw sustenance ceased to receive flow, there remained during the time of the Flood, in no force in the world, any flow but in the central line alone. And this is what David said (Psalms 29:10): ״ה׳ למבול ישב וישב ה׳ מלך לעולם״. And the word ישב in this place means 'remained,' that is to say, He alone — and similar to it (Psalms 9:8–9): ״וה׳ לעולם ישב״. And this is the saying of our Rabbis, of blessed memory, that the Flood did not fall upon the land of Israel — that is to say, that the rain did not descend upon it from the heavens. Now behold, this is to the glory of the land and to its exaltedness, that the sluices of the heavens were not opened over it, nor were the fountains of the great deep cleaved beneath it, for it is the central line below, corresponding to the central line above. And understand this." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> וימח — 'he blotted out' — in this world; וימחו מן הארץ — 'they were blotted out from the earth' — for the world to come. This Midrash alludes to the earth mentioned in the verse בראשית. And I have already mentioned it there."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:11:06.967951902Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}